{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/201675-idigam-chronicle-weekly-discussion-hunting-grounds","id":201675,"title":"Idigam Chronicle Weekly Discussion: Hunting Grounds","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Werewolf: The Forsaken"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-07-18T18:42:13-07:00","id":201675,"title":"Idigam Chronicle Weekly Discussion: Hunting Grounds","content":"Found here: <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/choose-your-ground/\" target=\"_blank\">http://theonyxpath.com/choose-your-ground/</a> Stew speaks about what Hunting Grounds are for the Idigam Chronicle, and how the development blog will work going into the future.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Writer. Developer.</i> <b>World of Darkness</b> | <b>Chronicles of Darkness</b> | <b>The Trinity Continuum</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/156-bunyip","name":"Bunyip","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1880"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-18T23:01:12-07:00","id":201830,"title":"","content":"Boo, I was hoping we'd have th locations spoiled for us! This is the chapter I'm mosted excited for, oddly enough; it was the best part of B&amp;S for me. We know one of the three European locations is Bristol, we know the Japanese location is Tokyo, and we know the Australian location is in the middle of the Outback; that leaves two more European spots, two in the States, and one in the Middle East. Place your bets now!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-19T03:57:46-07:00","id":201949,"title":"","content":"Baghdad, Denver ( or wherever the Rockies book was) and.... Boston!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2861-nyx","name":"Nyx","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2861_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"261"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-19T05:03:46-07:00","id":201958,"title":"","content":"Bristol is one of mine, as is one of the other European Hunting Grounds. The Hunting Grounds were a <i>lot</i> of fun to write and I hope you guys and girls enjoy them <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyx</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/201675-idigam-chronicle-weekly-discussion-hunting-grounds?p=201949#post201949\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Baghdad, Denver ( or wherever the Rockies book was) and.... Boston!</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't think it's a massive spoiler to point out that Boston already has an entire Mage setting book about it and hence is probably an unlikely bet for a Hunting Ground <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Generally, expect new stuff that hasn't been already covered elsewhere, with the exception of Tokyo.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>- Chris Allen, Aberrant Line Developer, Freelance Writer<br /> <br /> \u200bLike my work? Feel like helping me stay supplied with tea? Check out my <b><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/acrozatarim\" target=\"_blank\">Patreon</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1757-acrozatarim","name":"Acrozatarim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-19T05:29:55-07:00","id":201989,"title":"","content":"Australia sounds good! I'm excited for the rest. <i>B&amp;S</i> really sealed the deal for <i>Vampire</i> with me, and while I appreciate the rules and powers-upgrades it's really the settings that are my favorite part of the book. They're little pre-packaged campaigns that I can instantly see play out.<br /> <br /> Oh, go deal with those vengeance spirits again. Oh look, azlu pretending to be spider spirits. Wait, what's this? What're Americans doing here? Oh shit an Idigam-thing-whatever! Signal the Dreaming!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/638-reseru","name":"reseru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar638_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1574"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-19T06:09:55-07:00","id":202001,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>reseru</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/201675-idigam-chronicle-weekly-discussion-hunting-grounds?p=201989#post201989\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Australia sounds good! I'm excited for the rest. <i>B&amp;S</i> really sealed the deal for <i>Vampire</i> with me, and while I appreciate the rules and powers-upgrades it's really the settings that are my favorite part of the book. They're little pre-packaged campaigns that I can instantly see play out.<br /> <br /> Oh, go deal with those vengeance spirits again. Oh look, azlu pretending to be spider spirits. Wait, what's this? What're Americans doing here? Oh shit an Idigam-thing-whatever! Signal the Dreaming!</div> </div> </div> </div>Thank you. Glad you like it. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Writer. Developer.</i> <b>World of Darkness</b> | <b>Chronicles of Darkness</b> | <b>The Trinity Continuum</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/156-bunyip","name":"Bunyip","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1880"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-19T09:27:14-07:00","id":202203,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyx</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/201675-idigam-chronicle-weekly-discussion-hunting-grounds?p=201949#post201949\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Denver ( or wherever the Rockies book was)</div> </div> </div> </div>I wish, but honestly the Rockies have more than enough material to work with already. Between the Manitou Springs QuickStart, the appendix in the original core book, Hunting Grounds: the Rockies, us Coloradans have plenty to draw from for locally set games. Much as I'd like to get even more, it really is time for somewhere else to get a chance.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-19T09:40:01-07:00","id":202207,"title":"","content":"I might like to see Texas have a hunting ground. Private property rights here are held sacrosanct, so it'd be a good way to highlight the possessiveness that Uratha feel for their territory.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/233-daydreamer","name":"Daydreamer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar233_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"193"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-19T09:49:23-07:00","id":202210,"title":"","content":"El Paso's been a setting I've been thinking about doing a write up for for a couple of gamelines. Might poke it over the seven week break.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-19T10:28:15-07:00","id":202230,"title":"","content":"Well, in Australia there are some of the most poisonous spiders, so a large presence of Azlu would be understandable.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/316-jesuncolo","name":"Jesuncolo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar316_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"493"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-19T10:49:31-07:00","id":202245,"title":"","content":"Here's hoping for Florida. I was a little disappointed to see no Africa or South/Central America. But I was pleased to hear about a Middle East locationI do suppose we are at least somewhat limited 