grounds?p=202267#post202267\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Choke-full of Pure, if Sacramento is any indicative (Hunting Grounds featured in The Pure book).</div> </div> </div> </div>Well i'll have to check it out then-somehow I never read that part of the Pure.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-19T12:51:13-07:00","id":202322,"title":"","content":"Santa Fe, he means.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-19T15:20:54-07:00","id":202426,"title":"","content":"Kinda intrigued by the implication that the Tribes are a European construct.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I call the Integrity-analogue the &quot;<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/822559-trying-to-understand-the-morality-system?p=825008#post825008\" target=\"_blank\">subjective stat</a>&quot;.<br /> An explanation how to <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/913221-using-social-manuevering\" target=\"_blank\">use Social Manuevering</a>.<br /> Guanxi Explanations: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/787518-the-mysterium-and-their-contribution-to-mage-society?p=787824#post787824\" target=\"_blank\">1</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/787518-the-mysterium-and-their-contribution-to-mage-society?p=788173#post788173\" target=\"_blank\">2</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/833863-mages-and-trading-favors?p=834531#post834531\" target=\"_blank\">3</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2758-errol216","name":"Errol216","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1112"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-19T16:18:40-07:00","id":202465,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Errol216</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/201675-idigam-chronicle-weekly-discussion-hunting-grounds?p=202426#post202426\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Kinda intrigued by the implication that the Tribes are a European construct.</div> </div> </div> </div>Kinda intrigued by one of the idigam crashing a UFO to earth.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-19T16:20:04-07:00","id":202467,"title":"","content":"I want to see some Oceania Hunting Grounds.<br /> <br /> Polynesia to be exact.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":604,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/604-shock","user":"Shock","date":". 07-19-2014, 07:22 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/604-shock","name":"Shock","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar604_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1071"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-19T16:53:45-07:00","id":202483,"title":"","content":"There is usually a logic, something thematic that resonates between the place and the game's themes, so what are the places which you think scream werewolf?<br /> <br /> <br /> Personally, I think that a lot of the weather we have had in the past year or so (polar vortex winter, superstorm Sandy...) Would give good resonance for urban areas like, say Long Island or New Jersey coming to terms with the decidedly raw deal of nature wrecking their stuff. With the barrier between civilization and nature weakened, why not between the two sides of the Gauntlet?<br /> <br /> New York City -looks- fine, but they are still doing subway repairs after millions of gallons of seawater filled a massive network of subway tunnels from floor to ceiling in some places.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3070-barbrarilen","name":"Barbrarilen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3070_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"268"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-19T16:58:55-07:00","id":202489,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Barbrarilen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/201675-idigam-chronicle-weekly-discussion-hunting-grounds?p=202483#post202483\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There is usually a logic, something thematic that resonates between the place and the game's themes, so what are the places which you think scream werewolf?<br /> <br /> <br /> Personally, I think that a lot of the weather we have had in the past year or so (polar vortex winter, superstorm Sandy...) Would give good resonance for urban areas like, say Long Island or New Jersey coming to terms with the decidedly raw deal of nature wrecking their stuff. With the barrier between civilization and nature weakened, why not between the two sides of the Gauntlet?<br /> <br /> New York City -looks- fine, but they are still doing subway repairs after millions of gallons of seawater filled a massive network of subway tunnels from floor to ceiling in some places.</div> </div> </div> </div>WoD: Chicago nailed the feel of urban Werewolf, dude. Pick it up if you haven't yet.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-19T17:03:38-07:00","id":202493,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Errol216</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/201675-idigam-chronicle-weekly-discussion-hunting-grounds?p=202426#post202426\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Kinda intrigued by the implication that the Tribes are a European construct.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's certainly <i>a</i> way to read the arrival of the tribes in one of the most distant continents from the supposed birthplace of humanity.<br /> <br /> I'd find the evidence that the tribes are new enough that an entire continent managed to have a werewolf population that lacked them more intriguing what it suggests about Pangaea, frankly.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-19T17:26:46-07:00","id":202500,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/201675-idigam-chronicle-weekly-discussion-hunting-grounds?p=202203#post202203\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I wish, but honestly the Rockies have more than enough material to work with already. Between the Manitou Springs QuickStart, the appendix in the original core book, Hunting Grounds: the Rockies, us Coloradans have plenty to draw from for locally set games. Much as I'd like to get even more, it really is time for somewhere else to get a chance.</div> </div> </div> </div>Amen to that one !!! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\">The problem with defending the purity of the English language is that English is about as pure as a cribhouse whore. We don't just borrow words; on occasion, English has pursued other languages down alleyways to beat them unconscious and rifle their pockets for new vocabulary. - James. D. Nicoll</span></span></i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/540-tymeaus-jalynsfein","name":"Tymeaus Jalynsfein","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"869"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-19T17:34:22-07:00","id":202504,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/201675-idigam-chronicle-weekly-discussion-hunting-grounds?p=202322#post202322\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Santa Fe, he means.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, brain fart, there. Thanks for the correction.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-19T18:50:20-07:00","id":202537,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/201675-idigam-chronicle-weekly-discussion-hunting-grounds?p=202493#post202493\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That's certainly <i>a</i> way to read the arrival of the tribes in one of the most distant continents from the supposed birthplace of humanity.<br /> <br /> I'd find the evidence that the tribes are new enough that an entire continent managed to have a werewolf population that lacked them more intriguing what it suggests about Pangaea, frankly.</div> </div> </div> </div>My understanding of early human migration patterns is that Australia was settled <i>before</i> Europe; that is, the Middle East -&gt; Europe migration was third wave, whereas the Africa -&gt; India -&gt; Australia was second wave. Wikipedia appears to back me up.<br /> <br /> I'm not sure what it suggests about Pangaea, though, but I'm not clear on how the timeline works between Pangaea-no-more, Gauntlet-comes-down, and Tribes-are-formed; there are a lot of possibilities to noodle over with that.<br /> <br /> ...incidentally, does <i>any</i> gameline mythology anticipate the existence of oceans? Mage's kinda does, depending on how you read it, but... I think that's it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I call the Integrity-analogue the &quot;<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/822559-trying-to-understand-the-morality-system?p=825008#post825008\" target=\"_blank\">subjective stat</a>&quot;.<br /> An explanation how to <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/913221-using-social-manuevering\" target=\"_blank\">use Social Manuevering</a>.<br /> Guanxi Explanations: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/787518-the-mysterium-and-their-contribution-to-mage-society?p=787824#post787824\" target=\"_blank\">1</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/787518-the-mysterium-and-their-contribution-to-mage-society?p=788173#post788173\" target=\"_blank\">2</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/833863-mages-and-trading-favors?p=834531#post834531\" target=\"_blank\">3</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2758-errol216","name":"Errol216","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1112"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-19T20:25:45-07:00","id":202578,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Errol216</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/201675-idigam-chronicle-weekly-discussion-hunting-grounds?p=202537#post202537\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My understanding of early human migration patterns is that Australia was settled <i>before</i> Europe; that is, the Middle East -&gt; Europe migration was third wave, whereas the Africa -&gt; India -&gt; Australia was second wave. Wikipedia appears to back me up.</div> </div> </div> </div>You appear to have confused my reference to &quot;the birthplace of humanity&quot; with your own reference to Europe. That's faintly depressing. I don't especially care when Europe was settled in comparison to the apparent fact you seem to have just missed picking up on: that by this measure <i>the tribes seem to post-date second-wave human migration.</i><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I'm not sure what it suggests about Pangaea, though, but I'm not clear on how the timeline works between Pangaea-no-more, Gauntlet-comes-down, and Tribes-are-formed; there are a lot of possibilities to noodle over with that. </div> </div> </div>It suggests that the formation of the tribes (and possibly the ascendancy of the Firstborn) was geographically and/or temporally involved in a fashion that the mythology of the Sundering itself does not necessitate, i.e. it indicates that either the formation of the Tribes of the Moon and possibly the Pure Tribes is a historical set of events rather than being rooted in mythic prehistory or there's something about Australia that made the Firstborn not bother reaching out to the Ghost Wolves of the Outback.<br /> <br /> And that is a more interesting line of questioning to me than &quot;why did colonialization and imperialism - forces which by definition bring people (and thus werewolves) from one place to another - bring philosophical-spiritual ideals associated with one group of werewolves to another?&quot;<br /> <br /> That it doesn't smack of tedious assumptions of Eurocentrism is another thing to recommend the former over the latter.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":111,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","user":"Satchel","date":". 07-19-2014, 11:28 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-19T20:36:15-07:00","id":202580,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Errol216</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/201675-idigam-chronicle-weekly-discussion-hunting-grounds?p=202537#post202537\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">...incidentally, does <i>any</i> gameline mythology anticipate the existence of oceans? Mage's kinda does, depending on how you read it, but... I think that's it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Werewolf gets a little, but most gamelines avoid giving any importance to oceans. They're there, that's about it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-19T22:02:03-07:00","id":202651,"title":"","content":"The things about oceans is that it's actually really hard to do stories highly centered on them because of the limits of what most people can do out there.<br /> <br /> Still, the Polynesian Islands would be an interesting setting. I'm not too sure how I feel about it as a Werewolf setting, but I'd like to see them.<br /> <br /> Ooh, Promethean might be an awesome game for it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-19T23:26:22-07:00","id":202684,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/201675-idigam-chronicle-weekly-discussion-hunting-grounds?p=202578#post202578\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You appear to have confused my reference to &quot;the birthplace of humanity&quot; with your own reference to Europe. That's faintly depressing. I don't especially care when Europe was settled in comparison to the apparent fact you seem to have just missed picking up on: that by this measure <i>the tribes seem to post-date second-wave human migration.</i></div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, your comment was really hard for me to parse. I thought you meant that it was strange Australia, which was further away, did not have the same tropes that Europe, which was closer, did, since any trope would have a larger distance to travel. I have no idea how you managed to get &quot;I think Europe was the birthplace of humanity&quot; out of my comment.<br /> <br /> You are right; the implication about when the tribes formed <i>is</i> an interesting detail that I missed. Next to that, though, is the bit in Stew's post where he mentions a large Lodge of Ghost Wolves with aspirations of becoming a Tribe. Which is fairly in-keeping with the trend of &quot;y-splats are mutable&quot; that B&amp;S and FWC have already been indicating.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/201675-idigam-chronicle-weekly-discussion-hunting-grounds?p=202578#post202578\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And that is a more interesting line of questioning to me than &quot;why did colonialization and imperialism - forces which by definition bring people (and thus werewolves) from one place to another - bring philosophical-spiritual ideals associated with one group of werewolves to another?&quot;<br /> <br /> That it doesn't smack of tedious assumptions of Eurocentrism is another thing to recommend the former over the latter.</div> </div> </div> </div>I certainly agree that, if you frame the question in the least interesting way possible, it is very boring. Fortunately, I don't have your gift for that, nor the same grasp of history you do, so I'm free to wonder at what point the names Iron Masters or Ivory Claws start to make sense and where. Sumeria? China? Greece? Not the Americas. I can wonder whether or not, like Mage Orders, some of the present day Tribes are the result of unification, or if two present day Tribes were originally one. Perhaps the Storm Lords were Bone Shadows who got tired of the fixation on the Shadow, who felt mere shamanism wasn't sufficient for leadership anymore, and broke off. That might explain one of the founding Iminir myths where everyone else had tribal totems, but they had to then go seek out Skolis-Ur.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I call the Integrity-analogue the &quot;<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/822559-trying-to-understand-the-morality-system?p=825008#post825008\" target=\"_blank\">subjective stat</a>&quot;.<br /> An explanation how to <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/913221-using-social-manuevering\" target=\"_blank\">use Social Manuevering</a>.<br /> Guanxi Explanations: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/787518-the-mysterium-and-their-contribution-to-mage-society?p=787824#post787824\" target=\"_blank\">1</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/787518-the-mysterium-and-their-contribution-to-mage-society?p=788173#post788173\" target=\"_blank\">2</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/833863-mages-and-trading-favors?p=834531#post834531\" target=\"_blank\">3</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2758-errol216","name":"Errol216","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1112"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-19T23:39:56-07:00","id":202701,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Errol216</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/201675-idigam-chronicle-weekly-discussion-hunting-grounds?p=202684#post202684\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> You are right; the implication about when the tribes formed <i>is</i> an interesting detail that I missed. Next to that, though, is the bit in Stew's post where he mentions a large Lodge of Ghost Wolves with aspirations of becoming a Tribe. Which is fairly in-keeping with the trend of &quot;y-splats are mutable&quot; that B&amp;S and FWC have already been indicating.</div> </div> </div> </div> Actually that's nothing new, tribes of the moon talks about the issue of new tribes coming about, to simplify something that is epic in nature, all it takes to make a new tribe is to find some ghost wolves interested and find yourself a spirit worthy and interested in being your new tribal totem, it gives the idea of three new tribes: basically internal affairs for werewolves, a religious tribe so something like the pure but not you know insane, and I can't recall the third idea. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/391-stsword","name":"StSword","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar391_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1635"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-20T00:21:39-07:00","id":202717,"title":"","content":"This is much, much better than WtF's other attempt at Australian Urathra. It isn't racially tinged at all. <br /> <br /> It should be noted, The Dreaming isn't set in the past, like the Genesis story of the bible, but rather it's outside of time (or it's both the past, the present and the future). Theoretically, The Dreaming is happening right now. It's a hard concept to explain, because it's so removed from western thought. Secondly, the dreaming isn't a static entity, like the bible. New Dreamtime stories are formed all the time, and original stories undergo changes (with the westernization and conversion of the majority of Indigenous Australians has made this less common). Missionaries were not amused when Indigenous Australians inserted Jesus into the The Dreaming rather than converting.<br /> <br /> Secondly, Alice Springs is a dangerous place. It's one of the most dangerous places in the western world, if not the most dangerous place per capita. It's been nicknamed the stabbing capital of the world. It's a combination of extreme poverty and extreme and substance abuse. However, very rarely does this violence extend to the white or tourist population, and when it does it makes the headlines (ramps up the police presence as well). Two packs of Urathra could go at and as long as they don't kill anybody that matters and leave a dozen bodies on the ground, the police honestly would be hard pressed to notice any difference then normal.<br /> <br /> Secondly, you chose the Azlu over the Beshilu? <div class=\"videocontainer with-aspect-ratio videocontainer-horizontal\" style=\"aspect-ratio: 16/9;\"> <a class=\"video-frame\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=zWVw-j8eYSk\" data-code=\"zWVw-j8eYSk\" data-provider=\"youtube\" data-height=\"0\" data-width=\"0\" itemprop=\"video\"> <div class=\"videothumbnail\" style=\"\"> <img src=\"https://img.youtube.com/vi/zWVw-j8eYSk/maxresdefault.jpg\" alt=\"\" /> <div class=\"videothumbnailoverlay\"></div> </div> </a> </div><br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1072-theye1","name":"theye1","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1072_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"36"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-20T04:39:42-07:00","id":202818,"title":"","content":"I wish I could understand what everyone's discussing. Maybe it's 7:30am and I got out of work an hour ago, or maybe it's the syntax that posters are using that's confusing","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/638-reseru","name":"reseru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar638_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1574"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-20T04:44:52-07:00","id":202821,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Leliel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/201675-idigam-chronicle-weekly-discussion-hunting-grounds?p=202306#post202306\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I must say, love what you've done. <br /> <br /> Especially given how...poorly werewolf games have handled Aussie-land before (*cough*Rage Across Australia*hack*).<br /> <br /> This is more than enough to get the bad taste out of my mouth.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thank you.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Writer. Developer.</i> <b>World of Darkness</b> | <b>Chronicles of Darkness</b> | <b>The Trinity Continuum</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/156-bunyip","name":"Bunyip","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1880"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-20T04:59:37-07:00","id":202824,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>theye1</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/201675-idigam-chronicle-weekly-discussion-hunting-grounds?p=202717#post202717\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This is much, much better than WtF's other attempt at Australian Urathra. It isn't racially tinged at all.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thank you. Race isn't meant to be part of it.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>theye1</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/201675-idigam-chronicle-weekly-discussion-hunting-grounds?p=202717#post202717\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It should be noted, The Dreaming isn't set in the past, like the Genesis story of the bible, but rather it's outside of time (or it's both the past, the present and the future). Theoretically, The Dreaming is happening right now. It's a hard concept to explain, because it's so removed from western thought. Secondly, the dreaming isn't a static entity, like the bible. New Dreamtime stories are formed all the time, and original stories undergo changes (with the westernization and conversion of the majority of Indigenous Australians has made this less common). Missionaries were not amused when Indigenous Australians inserted Jesus into the The Dreaming rather than converting.<br /> <br /> Secondly, Alice Springs is a dangerous place. It's one of the most dangerous places in the western world, if not the most dangerous place per capita. It's been nicknamed the stabbing capital of the world. It's a combination of extreme poverty and extreme and substance abuse. However, very rarely does this violence extend to the white or tourist population, and when it does it makes the headlines (ramps up the police presence as well). Two packs of Urathra could go at and as long as they don't kill anybody that matters and leave a dozen bodies on the ground, the police honestly would be hard pressed to notice any difference then normal.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm not sure what points you're making here, but I'm happy to discuss if you want to clarify. Or possibly you're just seeking to inform?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>theye1</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/201675-idigam-chronicle-weekly-discussion-hunting-grounds?p=202717#post202717\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Secondly, you chose the Azlu over the Beshilu?</div> </div> </div> </div>(Thirdly?) Yes, rats aren't that common in Central Australia, whereas spiders are. (Admittedly, not too many are Azlu sized). Also, your video shows a mice plague.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Writer. Developer.</i> <b>World of Darkness</b> | <b>Chronicles of Darkness</b> | <b>The Trinity Continuum</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/156-bunyip","name":"Bunyip","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1880"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-20T06:18:36-07:00","id":202857,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bunyip</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/201675-idigam-chronicle-weekly-discussion-hunting-grounds?p=202824#post202824\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> I'm not sure what points you're making here, but I'm happy to discuss if you want to clarify. Or possibly you're just seeking to inform?</div> </div> </div> </div>Just clarifying. You talk a lot about what The Dreaming means to the Uratha. You don't talk about what The Dreaming <i>is</i>. I guess the closest comparison of The Dreaming is the concept of the soul in Christianity. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1072-theye1","name":"theye1","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1072_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"36"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-20T08:49:38-07:00","id":202992,"title":"","content":"Bunyip's other Hunting Ground is actually, to my mind, even cooler than his Alice Springs write-up <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> As for the lack of Africa and South America Hunting Grounds, yeah, the focus has been on making sure that we're writing about places that we are familiar with or have personal experience of, precisely to avoid the sort of mangled depiction of an area and its people that have sometimes occurred in the past. There's also that we each had a limited number of Hunting Grounds to write so, while some of the other writers might have the experience needed to do a South American or African location, they had to pick and choose which of their ideas they wanted to write up.<br /> <br /> Me, I've never been to South America and I've only been to Africa while very, very young. If I'd had a third Hunting Ground, I'd have done Bangkok, my place of birth.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>- Chris Allen, Aberrant Line Developer, Freelance Writer<br /> <br /> \u200bLike my work? Feel like helping me stay supplied with tea? Check out my <b><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/acrozatarim\" target=\"_blank\">Patreon</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1757-acrozatarim","name":"Acrozatarim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-20T09:41:20-07:00","id":203033,"title":"","content":"What are mentioned Waystones in context of Wolf-Blooded in the text? Is it now <b>Werewolf</b> name for concept similar to <b>Blood and Smoke</b> Touchstones? Persons and things guiding you in the direction of Flesh or Spirit?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-20T10:14:05-07:00","id":203053,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/201675-idigam-chronicle-weekly-discussion-hunting-grounds?p=203033#post203033\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What are mentioned Waystones in context of Wolf-Blooded in the text? Is it now <b>Werewolf</b> name for concept similar to <b>Blood and Smoke</b> Touchstones? Persons and things guiding you in the direction of Flesh or Spirit?</div> </div> </div> </div>Nice catch!<br /> <br /> Dunno tho.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-20T10:20:46-07:00","id":203055,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/201675-idigam-chronicle-weekly-discussion-hunting-grounds?p=203033#post203033\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What are mentioned Waystones in context of Wolf-Blooded in the text? Is it now <b>Werewolf</b> name for concept similar to <b>Blood and Smoke</b> Touchstones? Persons and things guiding you in the direction of Flesh or Spirit?</div> </div> </div> </div>They're not Touchstones, no.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>- Chris Allen, Aberrant Line Developer, Freelance Writer<br /> <br /> \u200bLike my work? Feel like helping me stay supplied with tea? Check out my <b><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/acrozatarim\" target=\"_blank\">Patreon</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1757-acrozatarim","name":"Acrozatarim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-20T11:09:04-07:00","id":203068,"title":"","content":"IIRC waystones are the markers along songlines, used for navigation and territory delineation. Uratha might make use of them to navigate the shadow.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/935-cleverest-of-things","name":"Cleverest of Things","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar935_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"650"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-20T11:49:10-07:00","id":203087,"title":"","content":"I assumed Waystones were the name for the &quot;use Wolf-blooded to shift into Shadow&quot; Tell.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>StSword</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/201675-idigam-chronicle-weekly-discussion-hunting-grounds?p=202701#post202701\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Actually that's nothing new, tribes of the moon talks about the issue of new tribes coming about, to simplify something that is epic in nature, all it takes to make a new tribe is to find some ghost wolves interested and find yourself a spirit worthy and interested in being your new tribal totem, it gives the idea of three new tribes: basically internal affairs for werewolves, a religious tribe so something like the pure but not you know insane, and I can't recall the third idea.</div> </div> </div> </div>Huh. I couldn't find this in the Tribes book, though I did find a reference that said Ghost Wolves were discussed in &quot;The Rage&quot;, which I have not read.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I call the Integrity-analogue the &quot;<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/822559-trying-to-understand-the-morality-system?p=825008#post825008\" target=\"_blank\">subjective stat</a>&quot;.<br /> An explanation how to <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/913221-using-social-manuevering\" target=\"_blank\">use Social Manuevering</a>.<br /> Guanxi Explanations: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/787518-the-mysterium-and-their-contribution-to-mage-society?p=787824#post787824\" target=\"_blank\">1</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/787518-the-mysterium-and-their-contribution-to-mage-society?p=788173#post788173\" target=\"_blank\">2</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/833863-mages-and-trading-favors?p=834531#post834531\" target=\"_blank\">3</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2758-errol216","name":"Errol216","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1112"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-20T18:00:53-07:00","id":203332,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/201675-idigam-chronicle-weekly-discussion-hunting-grounds?p=203033#post203033\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What are mentioned Waystones in context of Wolf-Blooded in the text? Is it now <b>Werewolf</b> name for concept similar to <b>Blood and Smoke</b> Touchstones? Persons and things guiding you in the direction of Flesh or Spirit?</div> </div> </div> </div>If I had to guess I would have to say they are the Wolf-Blooded that act as Loci for the purpose of crossing the Gauntlet.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/477-xenorath","name":"Xenorath","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar477_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"169"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-20T21:28:25-07:00","id":203477,"title":"","content":"Speaking of dangerous cities, any of the towns along the US-Mexico border could make for a very interesting (if politically charged) setting for Werewolf. The region seems like it would be a magnet for a lot of really unpleasant types of spirits, and on top of that you've got vast stretches of some of the most dramatic and inhospitable wilderness in the world in between the pockets of civilization.<br /> <br /> As for the Middle-Eastern location, Riyadh might be an interesting choice: a city of five and a quarter million right in the middle of the Arabian Desert. I could see it being a stronghold of the Forsaken besieged by crazy desert-dwelling Pure nomads. On the other hand, some place like Basrah might make sense considering that (as far as I recall) Sumerian was an inspiration for First Tongue.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3209,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3209-catdoom","user":"CatDoom","date":". 07-21-2014, 12:42 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3209-catdoom","name":"CatDoom","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"370"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-20T22:49:18-07:00","id":203540,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CatDoom</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/201675-idigam-chronicle-weekly-discussion-hunting-grounds?p=203477#post203477\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Speaking of dangerous cities, any of the towns along the US-Mexico border could make for a very interesting (if politically charged) setting for Werewolf. The region seems like it would be a magnet for a lot of really unpleasant types of spirits, and on top of that you've got vast stretches of some of the most dramatic and inhospitable wilderness in the world in between the pockets of civilization.</div> </div> </div> </div>Shadows of Mexico substantially covered this. <br /> <br /> Honestly, I change my mind. Azlu is probably a better choice, you could even explain some of the smaller Azlu, as Sydney funnel webs who were accidentally transported to Northern Territory. Unlikely, but not impossible. I would love a cane toad or rabbit host. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1072-theye1","name":"theye1","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1072_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"36"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-20T23:38:41-07:00","id":203573,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>theye1</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/201675-idigam-chronicle-weekly-discussion-hunting-grounds?p=203540#post203540\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Shadows of Mexico substantially covered this.<br /> <br /> Honestly, I change my mind. Azlu is probably a better choice, you could even explain some of the smaller Azlu, as Sydney funnel webs who were accidentally transported to Northern Territory. Unlikely, but not impossible. I would love a cane toad or rabbit host.</div> </div> </div> </div>A rabbit host would be... interesting to say none the less. Considering how fast rabbits reproduce.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/604-shock","name":"Shock","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar604_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1071"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-21T00:42:24-07:00","id":203596,"title":"","content":"Crazy idea, but what about Detroit as a setting. Chicago may have covered Urban werewolves, but Detroit is a city like no other. Crazy weather lately, mass urban decay, wilderness reclaiming sections, gangs growing to be almost institutions, plus the border with Canada, the regrowth efforts, reform movements, and the tense atmosphere make Detroit the sort of place I could see werewolves stalking through.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2861-nyx","name":"Nyx","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2861_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"261"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-21T00:58:26-07:00","id":203604,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Acrozatarim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/201675-idigam-chronicle-weekly-discussion-hunting-grounds?p=202992#post202992\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Bunyip's other Hunting Ground is actually, to my mind, even cooler than his Alice Springs write-up <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>Very nice of you to say so, thanks. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Writer. Developer.</i> <b>World of Darkness</b> | <b>Chronicles of Darkness</b> | <b>The Trinity Continuum</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/156-bunyip","name":"Bunyip","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1880"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-21T00:58:50-07:00","id":203605,"title":"","content":"Detroit's essentially been considered the nearest thing Promethean has to a signature city, to my understanding, ever since it was the first unborrowed city to show up in the gameline's running chronicle. I think it fits that game a little better, broadly speaking.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-21T01:00:35-07:00","id":203610,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>theye1</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/201675-idigam-chronicle-weekly-discussion-hunting-grounds?p=202857#post202857\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Just clarifying. You talk a lot about what The Dreaming means to the Uratha. You don't talk about what The Dreaming <i>is</i>. I guess the closest comparison of The Dreaming is the concept of the soul in Christianity.</div> </div> </div> </div>Fair enough. That's word count, I'm afraid. What the Dreaming means to Uratha is more relevant to the Idigam Chronicle than what the concept of the Dreaming is. People may have to go online for that one.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Writer. Developer.</i> <b>World of Darkness</b> | <b>Chronicles of Darkness</b> | <b>The Trinity Continuum</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/156-bunyip","name":"Bunyip","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1880"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-21T01:03:13-07:00","id":203614,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Errol216</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/201675-idigam-chronicle-weekly-discussion-hunting-grounds?p=203087#post203087\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I assumed Waystones were the name for the &quot;use Wolf-blooded to shift into Shadow&quot; Tell.</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Xenorath</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/201675-idigam-chronicle-weekly-discussion-hunting-grounds?p=203332#post203332\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If I had to guess I would have to say they are the Wolf-Blooded that act as Loci for the purpose of crossing the Gauntlet.</div> </div> </div> </div>I can't confirm or deny anything due to NDA and fear of Stew, but those are interesting guesses.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Writer. Developer.</i> <b>World of Darkness</b> | <b>Chronicles of Darkness</b> | <b>The Trinity Continuum</b>","edited":{"userid":156,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/156-bunyip","user":"Bunyip","date":". 07-21-2014, 04:23 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/156-bunyip","name":"Bunyip","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1880"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-21T01:08:18-07:00","id":203615,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>theye1</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/201675-idigam-chronicle-weekly-discussion-hunting-grounds?p=203540#post203540\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Honestly, I change my mind. Azlu is probably a better choice, you could even explain some of the smaller Azlu, as Sydney funnel webs who were accidentally transported to Northern Territory. Unlikely, but not impossible. I would love a cane toad or rabbit host.</div> </div> </div> </div>Never say never. If I get to expand Australia for Forsaken* I may just try and detail that.<br /> <br /> * I have a mental map of what I think Australia would look like in the Forsaken setting. As well as most other nWoD settings. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Writer. Developer.</i> <b>World of Darkness</b> | <b>Chronicles of Darkness</b> | <b>The Trinity Continuum</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/156-bunyip","name":"Bunyip","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1880"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-21T01:16:42-07:00","id":203621,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyx</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/201675-idigam-chronicle-weekly-discussion-hunting-grounds?p=203596#post203596\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Crazy idea, but what about Detroit as a setting. Chicago may have covered Urban werewolves, but Detroit is a city like no other. Crazy weather lately, mass urban decay, wilderness reclaiming sections, gangs growing to be almost institutions, plus the border with Canada, the regrowth efforts, reform movements, and the tense atmosphere make Detroit the sort of place I could see werewolves stalking through.</div> </div> </div> </div>In my game it was the &quot;Mecca&quot; of the Lodge of Ruin.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-21T03:33:05-07:00","id":203706,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bunyip</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/201675-idigam-chronicle-weekly-discussion-hunting-grounds?p=203615#post203615\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Never say never. If I get to expand Australia for Forsaken* I may just try and detail that.<br /> <br /> * I have a mental map of what I think Australia would look like in the Forsaken setting. As well as most other nWoD settings. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>An expanded Hunting Grounds product would be a lot of fun to do.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>- Chris Allen, Aberrant Line Developer, Freelance Writer<br /> <br /> \u200bLike my work? Feel like helping me stay supplied with tea? Check out my <b><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/acrozatarim\" target=\"_blank\">Patreon</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1757-acrozatarim","name":"Acrozatarim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-21T04:05:27-07:00","id":203723,"title":"","content":"The mini settings in <i>Blood &amp; Smoke</i> were the highlight of that book for me, and it's looking to be the same for the Idigam Chronicle. Especially given how good <i>World of Darkness: Chicago</i> was, I'd love to see a few books full of nothing but settings across the globe for various lines. Seeing a few cities based around God-Machine mortals games would be a lot of fun (Night Vale has <i>screamed</i> God-Machine to me ever since its inception), and it would be nice to get content for games that might not be getting Chronicle books.<br /> <br /> The weirder the better, by the way. If OPP can manage to get away from the USA and the major cities of Western Europe without being offensive, then I want as much as you guys can dish out.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-21T04:44:26-07:00","id":203734,"title":"","content":"What I'd really like to see is a 2.0 of <i>WoD: Chicago </i>with the GMC rules and an overview of <b>all</b> the splats being there and how their politics intertwine. It's already established as a multi-splat setting in particular, so take it up to 11","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/638-reseru","name":"reseru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar638_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1574"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-21T06:56:47-07:00","id":203807,"title":"","content":"That book would be huge.<br /> <br /> Like, thicker than the dictionary.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-21T07:44:18-07:00","id":203842,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/201675-idigam-chronicle-weekly-discussion-hunting-grounds?p=203807#post203807\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That book would be huge.<br /> <br /> Like, thicker than the dictionary.</div> </div> </div> </div>Let me put it like this: break it into volumes and <i>never-ending stream of cash</i>.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I call the Integrity-analogue the &quot;<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/822559-trying-to-understand-the-morality-system?p=825008#post825008\" target=\"_blank\">subjective stat</a>&quot;.<br /> An explanation how to <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/913221-using-social-manuevering\" target=\"_blank\">use Social Manuevering</a>.<br /> Guanxi Explanations: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/787518-the-mysterium-and-their-contribution-to-mage-society?p=787824#post787824\" target=\"_blank\">1</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/787518-the-mysterium-and-their-contribution-to-mage-society?p=788173#post788173\" target=\"_blank\">2</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/833863-mages-and-trading-favors?p=834531#post834531\" target=\"_blank\">3</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2758-errol216","name":"Errol216","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1112"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-21T08:09:44-07:00","id":203852,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/201675-idigam-chronicle-weekly-discussion-hunting-grounds?p=203807#post203807\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That book would be huge.<br /> <br /> Like, thicker than the dictionary.</div> </div> </div> </div>It doesn't have to be any bigger than <i>Dark Eras</i> is going to end up being <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/638-reseru","name":"reseru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar638_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1574"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-21T09:41:48-07:00","id":203918,"title":"","content":"The old Chicago book is 422 pages, already well over the 320 initially (stretch goals will probably increase it) planned for Dark Eras. You'd free up some room getting rid of the adventures, which seem to be like around 14-17 pages each (there's three). But adding in the groups like Hunter and Changeling (probably the more populous and organized of splats) would tip it over 500. Then you have demon, promethean, and mummy, which likely aren't as populous but still would require some texts. Getting, maybe, 600-700 pages or so. Larger than w20, which is 550 pages. Closer to M20, which is 600+ pages. And I forgot the sin-eaters.<br /> <br /> It would be simpler to divvy it up into different books, while still mentioning the connections (Olivia Citysmith has a deal with Prince Maxwell, who's that? better get that other book). I'd expect some complaints from that, but at some point the connections would fade away, there's no reason to believe every supernatural knows about every other supernatural, or even a majority of them. Just warnings, 'Don't hang around Grand Central Station too much' and that kind of thing.<br /> <br /> Something like that would be great to see but it sounds like it'd be more of a luxury item (something that thick isn't going to be something everyone's going to get). It's been mentioned more than a few times on various threads about what books we'd like to see.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 07-21-2014, 01:03 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-21T22:54:04-07:00","id":204691,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Errol216</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/201675-idigam-chronicle-weekly-discussion-hunting-grounds?p=203087#post203087\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I assumed Waystones were the name for the &quot;use Wolf-blooded to shift into Shadow&quot; Tell.<br /> <br /> Huh. I couldn't find this in the Tribes book, though I did find a reference that said Ghost Wolves were discussed in &quot;The Rage&quot;, which I have not read.</div> </div> </div> </div> You are correct, it is indeed the Rage, so the idea of new tribes forming up is even older than I thought. I'm surprised more people haven't run with the idea.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/391-stsword","name":"StSword","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar391_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1635"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-22T05:40:20-07:00","id":204885,"title":"","content":"The Hunting Grounds were a lot of fun to write and a chance to take the Werewolf setting in some interesting directions, like the element of the Lodge angling to become a Tribe in my other Hunting Ground and the crazy awesomeness of Bunyip's other Hunting Ground. Once the book's out I might actually do a rough write-up for said Lodge in proper Tribal form as a potential 'what if?' result.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>- Chris Allen, Aberrant Line Developer, Freelance Writer<br /> <br /> \u200bLike my work? Feel like helping me stay supplied with tea? Check out my <b><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/acrozatarim\" target=\"_blank\">Patreon</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1757-acrozatarim","name":"Acrozatarim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-22T07:04:43-07:00","id":204911,"title":"","content":"If they became a tribe, what would they hunt?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/638-reseru","name":"reseru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar638_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1574"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-22T08:19:11-07:00","id":204968,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>reseru</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/201675-idigam-chronicle-weekly-discussion-hunting-grounds?p=204911#post204911\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If they became a tribe, what would they hunt?</div> </div> </div> </div>Idigam sounds like a cool idea...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-22T08:33:27-07:00","id":204978,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>reseru</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/201675-idigam-chronicle-weekly-discussion-hunting-grounds?p=204911#post204911\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If they became a tribe, what would they hunt?</div> </div> </div> </div>You'll have to wait and see <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>- Chris Allen, Aberrant Line Developer, Freelance Writer<br /> <br /> \u200bLike my work? Feel like helping me stay supplied with tea? Check out my <b><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/acrozatarim\" target=\"_blank\">Patreon</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1757-acrozatarim","name":"Acrozatarim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-22T09:07:45-07:00","id":205018,"title":"","content":"Angels. They hunt angels. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Eric Christian Berg</b><br /> <i>Onyx Path Freelancer</i><br /> Promethean: The Created Second Edition, Dark Eras Companion","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2019-eberg","name":"eberg","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2019_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"284"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-22T09:31:06-07:00","id":205043,"title":"","content":"i like eberg's idea.<br /> It would be cool to see the Forsaken's take on the god-machine and it's angels.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Freelance Writer: WtF Night Horrors: Shunned by the Moon<br /> United States Sailor, First Responder,Ally, Bad Speller, Book Hoarder and all around Nerd.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2640-rx781a","name":"rx781a","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2640_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"32"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-22T09:32:46-07:00","id":205047,"title":"","content":"Good heavens, no...nothing so easy.<br /> <br /> They Hunt Dreams.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Thoughts ripple out, birthing others","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1624-falleneco","name":"FallenEco","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1624_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1927"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-22T11:28:50-07:00","id":205167,"title":"","content":"Detroit seems like a good place to run urban Werewolf IMO.<br /> <br /> Though actually a Werewolf setting in one of the states with a smaller population and no big famous cities might be cool. Montana seems like it'd be good for that. It's got a strong First Nation presence that is supported by the state constitution so you've got plenty of cultural variation for characters to come from, it's a different kind of aesthetic from the usual Werewolf mid-west/deep south style and there's loads of wild space, mountains forests and so on, with various towns and villages scattered across it. Borders with Canada too, and that's always potentially useful for stories.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/117-solar","name":"Solar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar117_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1267"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-22T13:47:31-07:00","id":205309,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>eberg</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/201675-idigam-chronicle-weekly-discussion-hunting-grounds?p=205018#post205018\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Angels. They hunt angels. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Is this your way of telling me to write up Tribes each based around the hunt of another supernatural type within the World of Darkness? Because I think that's what you're saying to me right now.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-22T16:03:01-07:00","id":205420,"title":"","content":"That sounds pretty cool. I might suggest to the GM of my group's upcoming Idigam Chronicle's game to write up a lodge or two who's favored prey are other supernaturals within the city. Vampire Hunters, Hunter Hunters, it should be great fun!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3347-wild-eyes","name":"Wild-Eyes","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"121"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-22T16:08:08-07:00","id":205422,"title":"","content":"I think vampires will likely fit under human, with hunters, for the Iron Masters favored prey.<br /> Possibly hosts.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-22T16:11:42-07:00","id":205425,"title":"","content":"That was something I had actually been thinking about a bit. You figure, the reason the Iron Masters favored prey is humans, is because they are clever enough to test their own minds. What then of vampires and changlings? Supernatural creatures with most of the free will, and all of the intelligence of a mortal human?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3347-wild-eyes","name":"Wild-Eyes","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"121"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-22T16:40:21-07:00","id":205437,"title":"","content":"I suppose if changelings were going to fit under anything it'd be humans. Their Mask is hard to penetrate and, when it comes down to it, they are humans, just twisted by an external force. I don't think they're common enough to be a specific prey for an entire tribe.<br /> <br /> Vampires would fit under humans, as well. I don't know where, but I keep thinking they had some theories of vampires as some sort of obscure host, so they might fit there too. While I'm at least sure there'd be a stereotype that insinuates they're open prey for someone, I don't think there's a specific vampire-hunting tribe.<br /> <br /> Hunters are...human. Iron Masters. As for why, I'm not sure. It may be that since the Iron Masters stick close to human civilization they are more aware of the danger humanity can present. I'm really looking forward to seeing them, whatever they are, it seems like the character I'm planning to play would fit in there.<br /> <br /> But like everyone is saying, lodges can do that sort of thing. Turning a broad view into a sharp focus (we already have a vampire hunting lodge, the Lodge of the Willow Branch). Or a sharp focus into a broader view (the Lodge of the Shield who have to do things they wouldn't normally be trained to by their tribe to get their lodge business done). I suppose the important thing to remember is that the sacred prey is not the only prey. A Storm Lord can and will hunt down other threats than the Claimed. As I understand it they just have some powers that can give them an edge against the Claimed, and usually view Claimed as a more vital threat.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-22T19:04:49-07:00","id":205518,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Wild-Eyes</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/201675-idigam-chronicle-weekly-discussion-hunting-grounds?p=205420#post205420\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hunter Hunters</div> </div> </div> </div>My head asplode","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/638-reseru","name":"reseru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar638_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1574"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-24T08:57:35-07:00","id":207152,"title":"","content":"In my long-running WtF campaign set in San Francisco, there was a wee pack that was dedicated to hunting Vampires. Think Supernatural's Winchester brothers, but werewolves. The PCs spent a lot of time dealing with the fallout of their actions. Politically, they were very bad for Vampire-Werewolf relations. Of course, it was hard for the PCs to argue with the worthiness of their cause. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Eric Christian Berg</b><br /> <i>Onyx Path Freelancer</i><br /> Promethean: The Created Second Edition, Dark Eras Companion","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2019-eberg","name":"eberg","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2019_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"284"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-24T09:01:34-07:00","id":207174,"title":"","content":"Black Moon eXtreme 4evr. Bushwacked is GOAT.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-24T09:11:54-07:00","id":207216,"title":"","content":"The exact position that various supernaturals fall under the Tribal interests very much depends on the local expressions of the Tribes.<br /> <br /> For example, take vampires:<br /> - In one region, the Bone Shadows may consider vampires their prey. The Shadows might normally concern themselves with spirits, but they are also the traditional masters of the Gift of Death, and thus may consider the undead as falling within their portfolio. They might also argue that vampires are clearly related to spirits in some way - after all, there are these wierd ephemeral owl-things that tend to appear around them, and vampires have some sort of spirit inside them that drives them to bestial behaviour.<br /> - In another region, the Storm Lords consider vampires their prey. Vampires are clearly some sort of Claimed, after all - possessed corpses that are being puppeted by spirits that have broken the Great Wolf's law and breached the Gauntlet. That they act in a different way to other Claimed just means that they're a special sub-type, perhaps a stable 'breed' that has evolved a particular pattern of survival-behaviour. Whenever a vampire 'makes' another vampire, they actually use the Death Essence created by the killing to forge a new death or hunger spirit and ram it into the 'new' vampire's corpse.<br /> - In yet another region, the Iron Masters claim vampires as their prey. Whatever vampires may be, they stem from humankind and still act in - and through - humanity to a considerable degree. To hunt a vampire you need to know how to hunt a human - in particular you need to know the human that the vampire was and, to some extent, still is. You can't treat a vampire infestation the same way as you would deal with a Claimed invasion - you need a different toolset, a toolset the Iron Masters have.<br /> - In one particular region in Eastern Europe, it is the Blood Talons' sacred duty to hunt vampires. Local lore holds that vampires are evil spirits created from the souls of dead werewolves who were evil in life or who died in anguish; in short, werewolves create vampires. Since the Blood Talons are the ones who end werewolves' lives, it is their duty to ensure that the dead are sent off appropriately, preventing their restless spirits from rising again. When a vampire <i>is</i> detected, it's the Blood Talons who know that they have failed, that one of the dead People was not placated appropriately, and they must make good on their duty by dealing with it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>- Chris Allen, Aberrant Line Developer, Freelance Writer<br /> <br /> \u200bLike my work? Feel like helping me stay supplied with tea? Check out my <b><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/acrozatarim\" target=\"_blank\">Patreon</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1757-acrozatarim","name":"Acrozatarim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-28T02:18:19-07:00","id":210997,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Acrozatarim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/201675-idigam-chronicle-weekly-discussion-hunting-grounds?p=207216#post207216\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The exact position that various supernaturals fall under the Tribal interests very much depends on the local expressions of the Tribes.<br /> <br /> For example, take vampires:<br /> - In one region, the Bone Shadows may consider vampires their prey. The Shadows might normally concern themselves with spirits, but they are also the traditional masters of the Gift of Death, and thus may consider the undead as falling within their portfolio. They might also argue that vampires are clearly related to spirits in some way - after all, there are these wierd ephemeral owl-things that tend to appear around them, and vampires have some sort of spirit inside them that drives them to bestial behaviour.<br /> - In another region, the Storm Lords consider vampires their prey. Vampires are clearly some sort of Claimed, after all - possessed corpses that are being puppeted by spirits that have broken the Great Wolf's law and breached the Gauntlet. That they act in a different way to other Claimed just means that they're a special sub-type, perhaps a stable 'breed' that has evolved a particular pattern of survival-behaviour. Whenever a vampire 'makes' another vampire, they actually use the Death Essence created by the killing to forge a new death or hunger spirit and ram it into the 'new' vampire's corpse.<br /> - In yet another region, the Iron Masters claim vampires as their prey. Whatever vampires may be, they stem from humankind and still act in - and through - humanity to a considerable degree. To hunt a vampire you need to know how to hunt a human - in particular you need to know the human that the vampire was and, to some extent, still is. You can't treat a vampire infestation the same way as you would deal with a Claimed invasion - you need a different toolset, a toolset the Iron Masters have.<br /> - In one particular region in Eastern Europe, it is the Blood Talons' sacred duty to hunt vampires. Local lore holds that vampires are evil spirits created from the souls of dead werewolves who were evil in life or who died in anguish; in short, werewolves create vampires. Since the Blood Talons are the ones who end werewolves' lives, it is their duty to ensure that the dead are sent off appropriately, preventing their restless spirits from rising again. When a vampire <i>is</i> detected, it's the Blood Talons who know that they have failed, that one of the dead People was not placated appropriately, and they must make good on their duty by dealing with it.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm loving it! Could we see this example in <b>Idigam Chronicle</b> on crossovers, to show players later, please?<br /> <br /> But still, I suspect both Mages and Hunters to be Iron Masters thing - they are humans, only bit twisted by secrets from World of Darkness. Other supernatural are fair game for every Tribe based on local culture.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-29T01:31:52-07:00","id":212223,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Acrozatarim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/201675-idigam-chronicle-weekly-discussion-hunting-grounds?p=207216#post207216\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">- In one particular region in Eastern Europe, it is the Blood Talons' sacred duty to hunt vampires. Local lore holds that vampires are evil spirits created from the souls of dead werewolves who were evil in life or who died in anguish; in short, werewolves create vampires. Since the Blood Talons are the ones who end werewolves' lives, it is their duty to ensure that the dead are sent off appropriately, preventing their restless spirits from rising again. When a vampire <i>is</i> detected, it's the Blood Talons who know that they have failed, that one of the dead People was not placated appropriately, and they must make good on their duty by dealing with it.</div> </div> </div> </div>That is a beautiful use of the myths, born out of ignorance about actual vampires, but also very logical to the werewolves. That, and if there is a Gangel line in the area, it is very hard not to think that.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-15T10:58:23-07:00","id":229252,"title":"","content":"So, to necro this thread, I've been in Australia and I went to a museum or two. One thing they mentioned was... The Dreaming. How about that?<br /> <br /> I didn't get a lot of details, but now I know there must be a Wikipedia page, so to share: <a href=\"http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Dreaming_(spirituality\" target=\"_blank\">http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Dreaming_(spirituality</a>)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I call the Integrity-analogue the &quot;<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/822559-trying-to-understand-the-morality-system?p=825008#post825008\" target=\"_blank\">subjective stat</a>&quot;.<br /> An explanation how to <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/913221-using-social-manuevering\" target=\"_blank\">use Social Manuevering</a>.<br /> Guanxi Explanations: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/787518-the-mysterium-and-their-contribution-to-mage-society?p=787824#post787824\" target=\"_blank\">1</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/787518-the-mysterium-and-their-contribution-to-mage-society?p=788173#post788173\" target=\"_blank\">2</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/833863-mages-and-trading-favors?p=834531#post834531\" target=\"_blank\">3</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2758-errol216","name":"Errol216","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1112"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-15T14:24:13-07:00","id":229562,"title":"","content":"Sorry, I don't understand the question. What about the Dreaming? Can you expand and clarify, please?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Writer. Developer.</i> <b>World of Darkness</b> | <b>Chronicles of Darkness</b> | <b>The Trinity Continuum</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/156-bunyip","name":"Bunyip","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1880"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-19T06:16:20-07:00","id":234116,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/201675-idigam-chronicle-weekly-discussion-hunting-grounds?p=210997#post210997\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'm loving it! Could we see this example in <b>Idigam Chronicle</b> on crossovers, to show players later, please?<br /> <br /> But still, I suspect both Mages and Hunters to be Iron Masters thing - they are humans, only bit twisted by secrets from World of Darkness. Other supernatural are fair game for every Tribe based on local culture.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm not sure we'll have space to cover crossovers like this in the book, I'm afraid.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>- Chris Allen, Aberrant Line Developer, Freelance Writer<br /> <br /> \u200bLike my work? Feel like helping me stay supplied with tea? Check out my <b><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/acrozatarim\" target=\"_blank\">Patreon</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1757-acrozatarim","name":"Acrozatarim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-19T15:26:30-07:00","id":234721,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Acrozatarim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/201675-idigam-chronicle-weekly-discussion-hunting-grounds?p=207216#post207216\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The exact position that various supernaturals fall under the Tribal interests very much depends on the local expressions of the Tribes.<br /> <br /> For example, take vampires:<br /> - In one particular region in Eastern Europe, it is the Blood Talons' sacred duty to hunt vampires. Local lore holds that vampires are evil spirits created from the souls of dead werewolves who were evil in life or who died in anguish; in short, werewolves create vampires. Since the Blood Talons are the ones who end werewolves' lives, it is their duty to ensure that the dead are sent off appropriately, preventing their restless spirits from rising again. When a vampire <i>is</i> detected, it's the Blood Talons who know that they have failed, that one of the dead People was not placated appropriately, and they must make good on their duty by dealing with it.</div> </div> </div> </div>I totally thought you had made this up until I was reading a book about werewolves a couple weeks back and saw that basic idea.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/370-oriares","name":"Oriares","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar370_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"404"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-20T10:20:28-07:00","id":235536,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Errol216</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/201675-idigam-chronicle-weekly-discussion-hunting-grounds?p=229252#post229252\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, to necro this thread, I've been in Australia and I went to a museum or two. One thing they mentioned was... The Dreaming. How about that?<br /> <br /> I didn't get a lot of details, but now I know there must be a Wikipedia page, so to share: <a href=\"http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Dreaming_(spirituality\" target=\"_blank\">http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Dreaming_(spirituality</a>)</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah. I spent a semester in Australia myself - they have as much of a problem with their original inhabitants being displaced and their culture vaporized as anyone in the Americas did - the Dreaming is one of those things iconic enough to have survived, at least to a point, in spite of that. <br /> <br /> Every question I asked regarding aboriginal belief systems was.... Unsatisfactory? Or at least not answered well, maybe because the people I asked didn't know... But I essentially got the impression that the Dreaming was such a holistic experience that my uninformed question couldn't be answered accurately. A Very Big Deal.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3070-barbrarilen","name":"Barbrarilen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3070_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"268"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-20T10:35:26-07:00","id":235558,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Oriares</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/201675-idigam-chronicle-weekly-discussion-hunting-grounds?p=234721#post234721\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I totally thought you had made this up until I was reading a book about werewolves a couple weeks back and saw that basic idea.</div> </div> </div> </div>Indeed, there are areas of Europe wherein werewolf and vampire folklore are really tied very close together. You'll note that people quite often use terms like 'vrykolak' for vampires in various settings, fictions and so forth - vrykolak and its various sister words across several languages meaning, of course, 'werewolf' originally.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>- Chris Allen, Aberrant Line Developer, Freelance Writer<br /> <br /> \u200bLike my work? Feel like helping me stay supplied with tea? Check out my <b><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/acrozatarim\" target=\"_blank\">Patreon</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1757-acrozatarim","name":"Acrozatarim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-21T05:02:43-07:00","id":236335,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Barbrarilen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/201675-idigam-chronicle-weekly-discussion-hunting-grounds?p=235536#post235536\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yeah. I spent a semester in Australia myself - they have as much of a problem with their original inhabitants being displaced and their culture vaporized as anyone in the Americas did - the Dreaming is one of those things iconic enough to have survived, at least to a point, in spite of that. <br /> <br /> Every question I asked regarding aboriginal belief systems was.... Unsatisfactory? Or at least not answered well, maybe because the people I asked didn't know... But I essentially got the impression that the Dreaming was such a holistic experience that my uninformed question couldn't be answered accurately. A Very Big Deal.</div> </div> </div> </div>I still don't understand what the question is in relation to the Hunting Grounds, sorry.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Writer. Developer.</i> <b>World of Darkness</b> | <b>Chronicles of Darkness</b> | <b>The Trinity Continuum</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/156-bunyip","name":"Bunyip","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1880"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-21T09:30:09-07:00","id":236570,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bunyip</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/201675-idigam-chronicle-weekly-discussion-hunting-grounds?p=236335#post236335\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I still don't understand what the question is in relation to the Hunting Grounds, sorry.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sorry, I didn't have a question? I was just responding to Eroll's comment. I guess if I did have a question it would be about how deep the research is into history/culture/locales that was done for each hunting ground to make sure the writers weren't just flailing about, but I know you guys did your research, so I wasn't going to ask that? :-)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3070-barbrarilen","name":"Barbrarilen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3070_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"268"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-22T09:32:38-07:00","id":237076,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Acrozatarim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/201675-idigam-chronicle-weekly-discussion-hunting-grounds?p=234116#post234116\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm not sure we'll have space to cover crossovers like this in the book, I'm afraid.</div> </div> </div> </div>So maybe at least official blog post on crossover ideas like those for Hunting Grounds? This vampire stuff was real goldmine of ideas. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-22T20:59:00-07:00","id":237696,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Barbrarilen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/201675-idigam-chronicle-weekly-discussion-hunting-grounds?p=236570#post236570\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sorry, I didn't have a question? I was just responding to Eroll's comment. I guess if I did have a question it would be about how deep the research is into history/culture/locales that was done for each hunting ground to make sure the writers weren't just flailing about, but I know you guys did your research, so I wasn't going to ask that? :-)</div> </div> </div> </div>Thanks Barbrarilen. I was continuing on from when Errol216 said:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Errol216</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/201675-idigam-chronicle-weekly-discussion-hunting-grounds?p=229252#post229252\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, to necro this thread, I've been in Australia and I went to a museum or two. One thing they mentioned was... The Dreaming. How about that?<br /> <br /> I didn't get a lot of details, but now I know there must be a Wikipedia page, so to share: <a href=\"http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Dreaming_(spirituality\" target=\"_blank\">http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Dreaming_(spirituality</a>)</div> </div> </div> </div>My question relates to what was he asking when he said 'The Dreaming. How about that?' I'd be keen to answer if I understood what he wanted from that question. I thought from your response that you may have understood and that I was just having difficulty parsing something.<br /> <br /> To answer your follow-up question though, I've had quite a bit of experience with the culture, and did more research into it before I wrote the Hunting Ground. Happy to answer specifics if people have questions, with the caveat that NDAs still apply.<br /> <br /> <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Writer. Developer.</i> <b>World of Darkness</b> | <b>Chronicles of Darkness</b> | <b>The Trinity Continuum</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/156-bunyip","name":"Bunyip","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1880"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-22T21:05:15-07:00","id":237719,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bunyip</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/201675-idigam-chronicle-weekly-discussion-hunting-grounds?p=237696#post237696\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My question relates to what was he asking when he said 'The Dreaming. How about that?' I'd be keen to answer if I understood what he wanted from that question.</div> </div> </div> </div>The question, like its neighbor &quot;What are the odds?&quot;, would seem to be rhetorical.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-22T21:09:48-07:00","id":237741,"title":"","content":"That's pretty much the conclusion I had come to, but I don't want anyone to think I'm ignoring their questions.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Writer. Developer.</i> <b>World of Darkness</b> | <b>Chronicles of Darkness</b> | <b>The Trinity Continuum</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/156-bunyip","name":"Bunyip","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1880"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-29T06:57:19-07:00","id":243858,"title":"","content":"I just reread the preview, actually read the bit about <b>The Gap</b> this time. Can I say that I love the story hooks you guys have been putting in these books? I'm even more jazzed to check out the Hunting Grounds in the full book now. Why isn't it out yet? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127887-doing-first-tongue-translations?p=484226#post484226\" target=\"_blank\">Nihhina kalekal-zidu kal masun, kal manudanadu. Nihhina kalekal-zidu nukal shaghu-desasudu \u2014 nihhina kalekal-zidu kal innu-desasudu udhkal samm</a>.&quot; Arthur Ashe<br /> She/her, contributing writer for <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/363404/Scion-Pride-2021\" target=\"_blank\">Scion: Pride 2021</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1923-bigdamnhero","name":"BigDamnHero","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1923_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1263"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-29T07:08:12-07:00","id":243884,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BigDamnHero</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/201675-idigam-chronicle-weekly-discussion-hunting-grounds?p=243858#post243858\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I just reread the preview, actually read the bit about <b>The Gap</b> this time. Can I say that I love the story hooks you guys have been putting in these books? I'm even more jazzed to check out the Hunting Grounds in the full book now. Why isn't it out yet? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>Your time machine is broken? Personally, I am finding it a fascinating read, especially the bit on page [ REDACTED ].","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3070-barbrarilen","name":"Barbrarilen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3070_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"268"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-29T07:24:17-07:00","id":243902,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Barbrarilen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/201675-idigam-chronicle-weekly-discussion-hunting-grounds?p=243884#post243884\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Your time machine is broken? Personally, I am finding it a fascinating read, especially the bit on page [ REDACTED ].</div> </div> </div> </div>Too much Havoc build up on my time machine. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> Now I'm stuck in August 2014, advancing at a rate of 1 second per second. It's very irritating.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127887-doing-first-tongue-translations?p=484226#post484226\" target=\"_blank\">Nihhina kalekal-zidu kal masun, kal manudanadu. Nihhina kalekal-zidu nukal shaghu-desasudu \u2014 nihhina kalekal-zidu kal innu-desasudu udhkal samm</a>.&quot; Arthur Ashe<br /> She/her, contributing writer for <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/363404/Scion-Pride-2021\" target=\"_blank\">Scion: Pride 2021</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1923-bigdamnhero","name":"BigDamnHero","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1923_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1263"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-29T07:45:36-07:00","id":243925,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BigDamnHero</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/201675-idigam-chronicle-weekly-discussion-hunting-grounds?p=243902#post243902\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Too much Havoc build up on my time machine. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> Now I'm stuck in August 2014, advancing at a rate of 1 second per second. It's very irritating.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hit it with some sort of temporal crowbar. Or ask really nicely, maybe we will get some sort of timey-wimey Gifts to help you out.<br /> <br /> Time travelling sounds like an even more terrifying prospect when you add Uratha. I can't even say why, specifically.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3070-barbrarilen","name":"Barbrarilen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3070_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"268"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-29T08:11:22-07:00","id":243974,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Barbrarilen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/201675-idigam-chronicle-weekly-discussion-hunting-grounds?p=243925#post243925\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hit it with some sort of temporal crowbar.</div> </div> </div> </div><img src=\"https://dl.dropboxusercontent.com/u/4464486/148px-Crowbar_2557.png\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/><br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Time travelling sounds like an even more terrifying prospect when you add Uratha. I can't even say why, specifically. </div> </div> </div>Lodge of Tindalos, tho.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-29T08:15:36-07:00","id":243976,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/201675-idigam-chronicle-weekly-discussion-hunting-grounds?p=243974#post243974\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Lodge of Tindalos, tho.</div> </div> </div> </div>Works for me.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>- Chris Allen, Aberrant Line Developer, Freelance Writer<br /> <br /> \u200bLike my work? Feel like helping me stay supplied with tea? Check out my <b><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/acrozatarim\" target=\"_blank\">Patreon</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1757-acrozatarim","name":"Acrozatarim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-29T08:19:24-07:00","id":243979,"title":"","content":"As much as part of me is pleased with the idea of time-travelling werewolves, I must remind you that the True Brujah exist as a warning against just slapping 'time-travelling' on any old creature is <i>kind</i> <i>of</i> a bad idea.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-29T08:21:22-07:00","id":243980,"title":"","content":"@satchel thanks for getting the reference.... But as my splat-fu is weak, I don't know what Tindalos is <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> @AA bruja... That's from Vampire? Aw, come on, what's the WORST that could happen?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3070-barbrarilen","name":"Barbrarilen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3070_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"268"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-29T08:37:16-07:00","id":243988,"title":"","content":"It's a reference to the Hounds of Tindalos, some vagely canine creatures from the end (beggining?) of time that will, well, <i>hound</i> you if they catch a glimpse of you looking trough the tides of space-time.<br /> <br /> They are part of the Cthulu Mythos and they appear in the eponym short story.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><b>I</b>'m <b>S</b>o <b>M</b>eta <b>E</b>ven <b>T</b>his <b>A</b>cronym</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/195-thorbes","name":"Thorbes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar195_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2982"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-29T08:38:44-07:00","id":243990,"title":"","content":"Ohhhhhhh. That. Thank you!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3070-barbrarilen","name":"Barbrarilen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3070_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"268"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-29T08:55:48-07:00","id":244022,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Barbrarilen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/201675-idigam-chronicle-weekly-discussion-hunting-grounds?p=243980#post243980\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">@AA bruja... That's from Vampire? Aw, come on, what's the WORST that could happen?</div> </div> </div> </div>You don't wanna know.<br /> <br /> If it plays out anything like that, <i><b>I am dead serious</b></i>, I will <i>abandon </i>the Forsaken ship.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>- If you must be ridiculous, I must ridicule you.<br /> - Those that can give up essential liberties in exchange for temporary safety deserve neither liberty nor safety. -- Benjamin Franklin</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/375-papa-bear","name":"Papa Bear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar375_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1920"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-29T11:19:22-07:00","id":244201,"title":"","content":"The core of the Hounds of Tindalos has been them hunting down trespassers of their territory, time. Whether they exist in angled time, while we live in curved time or they exist in the another dimension (that of time) or something else depends on the writer at the time. When hunting prey, they require angles to seep through, and &quot;a person kept in a perfectly round room would be safe from the beast's attack.&quot;<br /> <br /> Anyways, they hunt time travelers. Anyone moving faster than 1 hour per hour, or in a different direction.<br /> <br /> Considering what we know of new Uratha, it wouldn't be that hard (or game-breaking) to make a Lodge based around wolves who've, in some way, contacted some strange spirit of time and exist to hunt people who meddle with time. They wouldn't need time-travel powers to do this. Perhaps some power to let them slip through angles, but may affect them strangely (the Hounds are traditionally freaky looking).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-29T15:54:14-07:00","id":244388,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BigDamnHero</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/201675-idigam-chronicle-weekly-discussion-hunting-grounds?p=243858#post243858\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I just reread the preview, actually read the bit about <b>The Gap</b> this time. Can I say that I love the story hooks you guys have been putting in these books? I'm even more jazzed to check out the Hunting Grounds in the full book now. Why isn't it out yet? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>Thanks. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> The book progresses through the system. We've all submitted final drafts and now wait for what comes next.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Writer. Developer.</i> <b>World of Darkness</b> | <b>Chronicles of Darkness</b> | <b>The Trinity Continuum</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/156-bunyip","name":"Bunyip","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1880"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-29T17:53:40-07:00","id":244431,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bunyip</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/201675-idigam-chronicle-weekly-discussion-hunting-grounds?p=244388#post244388\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Thanks. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> The book progresses through the system. We've all submitted final drafts and now wait for what comes next.</div> </div> </div> </div>As a self proclaimed time traveller, I must say that the book was amazing and singlehandedly responsible for the establishment of the independent kingdom of Urathia now located in the middle of the Pacific. It has a GDP of $4.2 billion mostly due to tourists who wish to see the sculpture garden up close and personal.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/444-dessembrae","name":"Dessembrae","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar444_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"362"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-29T22:32:43-07:00","id":244549,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Papa Bear</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/201675-idigam-chronicle-weekly-discussion-hunting-grounds?p=244022#post244022\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You don't wanna know.<br /> <br /> If it plays out anything like that, <i><b>I am dead serious</b></i>, I will <i>abandon </i>the Forsaken ship.</div> </div> </div> </div>What was it you said? I <i>always</i> make fun of time travelling vampires?<br /> <br /> The absurdity of time travelling werewolves is somehow doubled.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-30T00:38:04-07:00","id":244618,"title":"","content":"I could see merit in a standalone supplement about time traveling werewolves. As long as people realised it wasn't part of the main canon. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Writer. Developer.</i> <b>World of Darkness</b> | <b>Chronicles of Darkness</b> | <b>The Trinity Continuum</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/156-bunyip","name":"Bunyip","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1880"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-30T03:45:14-07:00","id":244704,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bunyip</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/201675-idigam-chronicle-weekly-discussion-hunting-grounds?p=244618#post244618\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I could see merit in a standalone supplement about time traveling werewolves. <b>As long as people realised it wasn't part of the main canon. </b><img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>Because <i>that</i> would happen.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-30T05:28:03-07:00","id":244745,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/201675-idigam-chronicle-weekly-discussion-hunting-grounds?p=244549#post244549\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What was it you said? I <i>always</i> make fun of time travelling vampires?<br /> <br /> The absurdity of time travelling werewolves is somehow doubled.</div> </div> </div> </div>Time traveling vampires and werewolves <i>should </i>be made fun of!<br /> <br /> People bitch about <i><b>OTHER </b></i>things not seeming to fit within the genre/themes/moods/etc. But all of the sudden, slap a Time Manipulation power on a vampire clan<i>and it's okay!!???!!!</i><br /> <br /> Na, don't think so. The only two splats that have any business meddling with time are mages and changelings, and even then, they always learn later that is was a <b>bad idea.</b>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>- If you must be ridiculous, I must ridicule you.<br /> - Those that can give up essential liberties in exchange for temporary safety deserve neither liberty nor safety. -- Benjamin Franklin</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/375-papa-bear","name":"Papa Bear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar375_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1920"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-30T06:39:20-07:00","id":244769,"title":"","content":"Awww. I, for one, am a huge fan of the True Brujah and Temporis. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.dropbox.com/s/ofii86boiyk38ng/DtDRandomForms.zip\" target=\"_blank\">Open the gates of Hell: Random Demon Generator.</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1X6qQzoAPrSRNzl3cQcMWasoPv3eK56sIlAOTeay61No/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Gather an army of Rage! Random Garou Generator.</a><br /> Shapeshifting Historian<br /> Writer - Werewolf: the Apocalypse, Werewolf: the Forsaken, Exalted 3e, TC: \u00c6on","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/167-nikink","name":"nikink","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"360"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-30T07:48:23-07:00","id":244790,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Papa Bear</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/201675-idigam-chronicle-weekly-discussion-hunting-grounds?p=244745#post244745\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Time traveling vampires and werewolves <i>should </i>be made fun of!<br /> <br /> People bitch about <i><b>OTHER </b></i>things not seeming to fit within the genre/themes/moods/etc. But all of the sudden, slap a Time Manipulation power on a vampire clan<i>and it's okay!!???!!!</i><br /> <br /> Na, don't think so. The only two splats that have any business meddling with time are mages and changelings, and even then, they always learn later that is was a <b>bad idea.</b></div> </div> </div> </div>I think there's some room for demons as well-at least, it seems like both Fallen and Descent have handled that decently.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-30T09:04:08-07:00","id":244833,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Papa Bear</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/201675-idigam-chronicle-weekly-discussion-hunting-grounds?p=244022#post244022\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You don't wanna know.<br /> <br /> If it plays out anything like that, <i><b>I am dead serious</b></i>, I will <i>abandon </i>the Forsaken ship.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm fairly sure I could do a Tindalos-style Lodge without it being anything like the True Brujah <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr c